{"violation_type":{"id":"tx-tac-746-5202-2","jurisdiction":"TX","state":"TX","code_system":"Texas Administrative Code, Title 26, Ch. 746","original_code":"746.5202(2)","title":"Emergency Preparedness Plan - Communication Procedures (26 TAC §746.5202(2))","short_title":"Emergency Preparedness Plan - Communication Procedures","severities":{"medium_high":28},"facility_ids":["tx-hhsc-1527380","tx-hhsc-135722","tx-hhsc-1261926","tx-hhsc-1090026","tx-hhsc-1256776","tx-hhsc-1338287","tx-hhsc-309243","tx-hhsc-1406020","tx-hhsc-321021","tx-hhsc-1388147","tx-hhsc-1359338","tx-hhsc-1417826","tx-hhsc-1264770","tx-hhsc-162616","tx-hhsc-1372203","tx-hhsc-1459393","tx-hhsc-1470675","tx-hhsc-208704","tx-hhsc-1502126","tx-hhsc-97569","tx-hhsc-1471122","tx-hhsc-1330124","tx-hhsc-255447","tx-hhsc-1445313","tx-hhsc-261706","tx-hhsc-1512654","tx-hhsc-1495099"],"first_date":"2021-12-16","last_date":"2026-08-03","typical_finding":"The emergency preparedness plan did not contain the emergency telephone number.","finding_variants":[{"text":"The emergency preparedness plan did not contain the emergency telephone number.","count":2},{"text":"The operation didn't have how they would relocate children 24 months and younger in the emergency preparedness plan.    Corrected:  When the director add in the emergency preparedness plan.","count":1},{"text":"The emergency preparedness plan did not include the following:    -How children will be evacuated or relocated to the designated safe area or alternate shelter, including specific procedures for evacuating and relocating children who are under 24 months of age who have limited mobility, or who otherwise may need assistance in an emergency, such as children who have mental, visual, or hearing impairments.  -How children in attendance at the time of the emergency will be accounted for at the designated safe area or alternate shelter.  -How your staff will evacuate and relocate with the essential documentation including:  (A)Parent and emergency contact telephone numbers for each child in care.  (B)Authorization for emergency care for each child in care.  (C)The child tracking system information for children in care.   -How your staff will continue to care for the children until each child has been released.  -How you will reunify the children with their parents as the evacuation, relocation, or sheltering/lock-down is lifted.","count":1},{"text":"The Emergency Preparedness Plan was evaluated and lacked the following written procedures: 1) The emergency telephone number that is on file with Child Care Regulation; and 2) How you will communicate with local authorities, parents, and Child Care Regulation.","count":1},{"text":"The emergency preparedness plan was missing the following items:  How children who have limited mobility, or who otherwise may need assistance in an emergency, such as children who have mental, visual, or hearing impairments will be evacuated or relocated to the designated safe area or alternate shelter,  How your staff will evacuate and relocate with the essential documentation,  How your staff will continue to care for thechildren until each child has been released.","count":1},{"text":"Operation does not have an emergency preparedness plan available for review.","count":1}],"topic":"supervision","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios","topic_evidence":"INFERRED","primary_severity":"medium_high","occurrence_count":28,"facility_count":27},"by_year":{"2021":1,"2022":7,"2023":6,"2024":5,"2025":7,"2026":2},"facilities":[{"id":"tx-hhsc-1388147","name":"Winners Children Academy","type":"center","authority":"TX HHSC","status":"licensed","city":"Houston","zip":"77099","address":"10950 Bissonnet St Ste A350","capacity":52,"age_groups":["infant","toddler","preschool","school_age"],"lat":29.674367492171,"lon":-95.572077240577,"inspections":46,"last_inspection":"2026-10-14","violations":42,"open_violations":0,"severe_violations":34,"occurrences_of_type":2,"open_of_type":0},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1527380","name":"