ave limited mobility, or who otherwise may need assistance in an emergency, such as children who have mental, visual, or hearing impairments will be evacuated or relocated to the designated safe area or alternate shelter,  How your staff will evacuate and relocate with the essential documentation,  How your staff will continue to care for thechildren until each child has been released.","topic":"fire","source_record_id":"1026319749","facility_name":"Crossridge Preschool Academy"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-97569-i20230125-v5","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-5202-2","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-97569-i20230125","facility_id":"tx-hhsc-97569","date":"2023-01-25","original_code":"746.5202(2)","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","severity_rank":2,"source_category":"Medium High","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2023-02-03","finding":"Emergency Preparedness Plan - Communication Procedures: The operations emergency preparedness plan was missing specific procedures for how they will communicate with local authorities (such as fire, law enforcement, emergency medical services, health department), parents and licensing.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026467894","facility_name":"Alamo Heights Presbyterian Church"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-255447-i20221108-v9","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-5202-2","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-255447-i20221108","facility_id":"tx-hhsc-255447","date":"2022-11-08","original_code":"746.5202(2)","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","severity_rank":2,"source_category":"Medium High","status":"corrected","status_label":"Corrected at inspection","finding":"Emergency Preparedness Plan - Communication Procedures: The operation's emergency preparedness plan did not include how children will be evacuated or relocated to the designated safe area or alternate shelter, including specific procedures for evacuating and relocating children who are under 24 months of age.      This deficiency was corrected during the inspection as this information was added to the emergency preparedness plan.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026344338","facility_name":"Union Christian Academy"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1417826-i20220907-v4","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-5202-2","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1417826-i20220907","facility_id":"tx-hhsc-1417826","date":"2022-09-07","original_code":"746.5202(2)","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","severity_rank":2,"source_category":"Medium High","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2022-09-12","finding":"Emergency Preparedness Plan - Communication Procedures: The following was missing from the emergency preparedness plan: How you will communicate with local authorities (such as fire, law enforcement, emergency medical services, health department), parents and us","topic":"fire","source_record_id":"1026275565","facility_name":"Better Beginnings Academy LLC"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1090026-i20220831-v2","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-5202-2","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1090026-i20220831","facility_id":"tx-hhsc-1090026","date":"2022-08-31","original_code":"746.5202(2)","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","severity_rank":2,"source_category":"Medium High","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2022-09-06","finding":"Emergency Preparedness Plan - Communication Procedures: The Emergency Preparedness Plan was evaluated and lacked the following written procedures: 1) The emergency telephone number that is on file with Child Care Regulation; and 2) How you will communicate with local authorities, parents, and Child Care Regulation.","topic":"fire","source_record_id":"1026375178","facility_name":"Water Oak Preschool"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1261926-i20220303-v1","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-5202-2","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1261926-i20220303","facility_id":"tx-hhsc-1261926","date":"2022-03-03","original_code":"746.5202(2)","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","severity_rank":2,"source_category":"Medium High","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2022-03-15","finding":"Emergency Preparedness Plan - Communication Procedures: The emergency preparedness plan did not include the following:    -How children will be evacuated or relocated to the designated safe area or alternate shelter, including specific procedures for evacuating and relocating children who are under 24 months of age who have limited mobility, or who otherwise may need assistance in an emergency, such as children who have mental, visual, or hearing impairments.  -How children in attendance at the time of the emergency will be accounted for at the designated safe area or alternate shelter.  -How your staff will evacuate and relocate with the essential documentation including:  (A)Parent and emergency contact telephone numbers for each child in care.  (B)Authorization for emergency care for each child in care.  (C)The child tracking system information for children in care.   -How your staff will continue to care for the children until each child has been released.  -How you will reunify the children with their parents as the evacuation, relocation, or sheltering/lock-down is lifted.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026265841","facility_name":"Treehouse Learning Center"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1388147-i20220209-v2","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-5202-2","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1388147-i20220209","facility_id":"tx-hhsc-1388147","date":"2022-02-09","original_code":"746.5202(2)","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","severity_rank":2,"source_category":"Medium High","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2022-02-28","finding":"Emergency Preparedness Plan - Communication Procedures: The Emergency Preparedness Plan was reviewed and did not include the following:    -Evacuation diagram  -Procedures for evacuating and relocating children who are under 24 months of age, who have limited mobility, or who otherwise may need assistance.  -The emergency telephone number that is on file with us.  - How you will communicate with local authorities (such as fire, law enforcement, emergency medical services, health department), parents and Child Care Regulation.   -How your staff will continue to care for the children until each child has been released.","topic":"fire","source_record_id":"1026473857","facility_name":"Winners Children Academy"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1388147-i20220126-2-v3","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-5202-2","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1388147-i20220126-2","facility_id":"tx-hhsc-1388147","date":"2022-01-26","original_code":"746.5202(2)","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","severity_rank":2,"source_category":"Medium High","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2022-02-09","finding":"Emergency Preparedness Plan - Communication Procedures: The Emergency Preparedness Plan was reviewed and did not include the following:    -Evacuation diagram  -Procedures for evacuating and relocating children who are under 24 months of age, who have limited mobility, or who otherwise may need assistance.  -The emergency telephone number that is on file with us.  - How you will communicate with local authorities (such as fire, law enforcement, emergency medical services, health department), parents and Child Care Regulation.   -How your staff will continue to care for the children until each child has been released.      -The operation has two relocation sites listed.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026244435","facility_name":"Winners Children Academy"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1264770-i20220112-v7","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-5202-2","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1264770-i20220112","facility_id":"tx-hhsc-1264770","date":"2022-01-12","original_code":"746.5202(2)","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","severity_rank":2,"source_category":"Medium High","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2022-02-03","finding":"Emergency Preparedness Plan - Communication Procedures: The emergency preparedness plan does not include the following information:  1. The emergency telephone number on file with Child Care Regulation  2. How you will communicate with local authorities and Child Care Regulation  3. How staff will evacuate with parent and emergency contact information, authorization for emergency medical care and the sign-in/sign-out logs.","topic":"fire","source_record_id":"1026373114","facility_name":"Armand Bayou Montessori School"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-135722-i20211216-v1","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-5202-2","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-135722-i20211216","facility_id":"tx-hhsc-135722","date":"2021-12-16","original_code":"746.5202(2)","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","severity_rank":2,"source_category":"Medium High","status":"corrected","status_label":"Corrected at inspection","finding":"Emergency Preparedness Plan - Communication Procedures: The operation didn't have how they would relocate children 24 months and younger in the emergency preparedness plan.    Corrected:  When the director add in the emergency preparedness plan.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026224921","facility_name":"Zion Lutheran Preschool"}]}
